course: dictionary
lesson: 11170
title: Windy: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Windy comes from wind, the moving air you feel on your face. A windy day is a day with a lot of wind blowing. «Fly a kite on a windy day» tells you the wind is strong enough to lift a kite into the sky.
explain: A windy place is a place where the wind blows a lot, like a hilltop. The clue is the place word: hilltops are open, so the wind reaches them easily.
explain: A windy road is a road that bends a lot. It comes from «wind», as in turn, and is said WINE-dee. To check which meaning fits, put it into the sentence. If the sentence is about weather, windy means wind blowing.
fact: Windy is an adjective: windy, windier, windiest.
fact: «Windy weather» means weather with a lot of wind blowing.
fact: Windy is a weather word, like sunny, rainy and cloudy.
fact: «Il y a du vent» is French for «it's windy». Il y a means «there is», and du vent means «some wind».
fact: On dry, windy days, hay fever can get worse, because the wind blows more pollen about.
exercise: «Fly a kite on a windy day.» What does windy mean in this sentence? | A wet and grey sky | *Lots of wind blowing | A road that bends a lot | Hot and dry, with no breeze
exercise: «Il y a du vent» is French. What does it tell you? | It's raining | *It's windy | It's sunny | It's cloudy
exercise: Which place is most likely to be windy? | *A hilltop, open to the sky | A dark cellar | A cosy cupboard under the stairs | A sealed jar on a shelf
test: «The windy road wound up the mountain, bending at every corner.» What does windy mean here? | Lots of wind blowing on the road | Closed for repairs | *A road that bends a lot | Very wide and flat
test: Why can hay fever be worse on windy days? | Wind makes people fall asleep | Wind makes the air too cold to breathe | Wind washes all the pollen away | *Wind blows more pollen about
exam: Which sentence uses windy to mean "bends a lot"? | «Wet washing dries on a line on a warm windy day.» | «Fly a kite on a windy day.» | *«The windy road curled round the hill.» | «Wildfires spread fast in dry, hot, windy weather.»
